/* :not(.nx-dark-island .glass) — the promo carousel's sheet is a `.glass`
   sitting over its OWN photographic artwork and scrim, tuned with literal
   pale-blue/white text throughout (never page tokens), same as a hero. The
   unscoped version of this rule turned it into a bright white pane with
   still-white text on top of it — invisible, not readable. */
html[data-theme="light"] .glass:not(.nx-dark-island .glass),
html[data-theme="light"] .glass-sm:not(.nx-dark-island .glass-sm) {
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.72);
  border-color: var(--color-rim);
  /* `.glass`'s box-shadow (the "liquid glass" block further down this file)
     is a set of literal insets tuned for a dark material: a near-opaque
     white line lighting the top edge, a broad white glow bleeding 18-32px
     into the body, and a 50%-black shadow weighting the bottom third. None
     of those are page tokens, so flipping to a white background above did
     nothing to them — the result was white-on-white glare at the top and a
     dirty grey smear at the bottom of every `.glass` panel in light mode
     (the mail reply composer's popout, reported as "washed out, hazy,
     frosted glass gone wrong on a light background"). Swapped for the same
     restrained lift `.card` gets in light mode: a hairline shadow plus a
     soft ink-tinted drop, no directional "light source" baked in. */
  box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.06), 0 20px 44px -22px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.28);
}
/* `.glass`'s ::before (a lens-edge hairline) and ::after (a top-third gloss)
   are both literal white-on-white gradients whose entire job is to catch
   light on a dark material — there is no light-mode equivalent to swap in
   short of inventing a new effect (which the rest of this file deliberately
   avoids), so they are switched off rather than left painting extra white
   haze over an already-white panel. `.glass-sm` never defined these two, so
   it needs no matching rule. */
html[data-theme="light"] .glass:not(.nx-dark-island .glass)::before,
html[data-theme="light"] .glass:not(.nx-dark-island .glass)::after {
  content: none;
}

